<title>NEW ZEALAND: CRICKET-NZ A BUILD BIG LEAD OVER ENGLAND.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NZ A BUILD BIG LEAD OVER ENGLAND.</headline>
<dateline>WANGANUI, New Zealand 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand A led England by 261 runs with six second innings wickets standing on Friday at close of play on the second day of their four-day cricket match.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>New Zealand A First innings 181 (M. Horne 64, C. Silverwood 6-44)</p>
<p>Second Innings 187-4 (L. Howell 51 not out)</p>
<p>England First Innings 107 (R. Irani 40, G. Allott 4-44, H. Davis 4-22)</p>
